# Newest first (content phase)

When markdown collections land, public lists (news, teaching notes, gallery, and so on) sort **newest `date:` first**.

## Rules (when collections exist)

- Every list-backed markdown file has a `date:` (the event or publish day, `YYYY-MM-DD`).
- Index pages use a shared sort helper (for example `src/lib/contentSort.ts` with `newestFirst()`).
- Playwright helpers read the same content sources as the site — do not hard-code titles in specs.

Foundational phase: no collections yet. Apply these rules when the content milestone adds `src/content/`.
